 "design_note": "Each arm/leg is animated as ONE RIGID unit (upper_arm+hand, or leg+foot, swinging together from a single shoulder/hip pivot) rather than a two-joint (shoulder+elbow / hip+knee) chain. The traced geometry is a single closed tapered contour per limb, not an open centerline - splitting it into independently-bending sub-parts would require cutting the traced outline and synthesizing new closing edges, which is exactly the kind of geometry alteration this task prohibits. Rigid-pendulum limb swinging is a standard, safe simplification for stylized walk cycles and guarantees zero risk of broken/disconnected joints.",
